Be Original (v1.0.0) is an Android media forensics and ground-truth verification application designed to analyze digital text and images for tampering, synthetic AI generation, scripted staging, and factual fabrication, while recovering the unedited baseline source.
Below is the complete official documentation package, separated into Non-Technical (Executive & Public Release) and Technical (Architecture, Engineering & DevOps) sections.
Part 1: Non-Technical Release Documentation (Executive & Public)
1. Product Overview & Value Proposition
In an era of deepfakes, viral misinformation, and AI-spun content, Be Original gives everyday users a single-tap authenticity check directly on their Android phone. Rather than merely labeling content as "fake" or "suspicious," Be Original goes a step further by reconstructing and citing the Original Ground Truth—returning the unedited quote, baseline historical fact, or primary origin link.
2. Core User Features (What the App Does)
* Overall Authenticity Scorecard (0–100%): A clear, color-coded trust rating (Green for Authentic, Amber for Manipulated/AI-Assisted, Red for Synthetic/Fabricated) that summarizes risk at a glance.
* 4-Pillar Verification Breakdown:
    1. Modification & Tamper Check: Detects whether an image has been spliced, photoshopped, or stripped of its camera history, or whether a quote has been selectively cut.
    2. AI Involvement Detector: Evaluates the likelihood that text was written by an LLM or an image was generated by a diffusion tool.
    3. Scripted vs. Spontaneous Meter: Analyzes structural and rhetorical cues to determine if a statement or transcript is organic or PR-staged/rehearsed.
    4. Factuality & Fabrication Check: Cross-references claims against verified records to flag misleading or fabricated assertions.
* Interactive Tamper Heatmap (ELA Toggle): Users can flip a switch on any submitted photo to view a visual Error Level Analysis heatmap, which highlights manipulated or pasted regions that were re-compressed differently from the rest of the image.
* "Recovered Original" Anchor Card: Displays the verbatim unedited quote, baseline fact, and primary source reference at the bottom of every scan.
* Native Android Share-Sheet Integration: Users do not need to open the app first—they can share suspicious text or images directly from WhatsApp, Chrome, X, or their Photo Gallery straight into Be Original for instant verification.
Part 2: Technical Documentation (Engineering & Architecture)
1. System Architecture
Be Original v1.0 utilizes a Serverless Hybrid Edge-to-Cloud Architecture. This balances immediate local pixel/header forensics on the Android device with multimodal cloud reasoning and grounding, eliminating the need to maintain dedicated backend servers during initial rollout.
Component Layer	Technology / Specification	Responsibility
Client OS & SDK	Android API 26+ (Min SDK 26, Compile/Target SDK 35)	Broad device compatibility across Android 8.0 through Android 15/16.
Language & Concurrency	Kotlin (JVM Target 11) + Kotlinx Coroutines (1.8.1)	Asynchronous Dispatchers.IO pipeline for non-blocking bitmap math and network calls.
UI Framework	Jetpack Compose (Material 3 Dark Theme)	Reactive single-activity state management (MainActivity.kt) with dynamic scorecard rendering.
On-Device Metadata Engine	AndroidX ExifInterface (1.3.7)	Extracts raw file headers (TAG_SOFTWARE, TAG_MAKE, TAG_MODEL, TAG_DATETIME_ORIGINAL) to detect stripped metadata or editing software signatures.
On-Device Pixel Forensics	Custom Bitmap ELA Engine (90% JPEG Re-compression, 20x Delta Amplification)	Calculates pixel-by-pixel RGB compression variance (elaVariance) and renders an ARGB_8888 heatmap overlay locally on the device CPU.
Cloud Verification & Recovery	Google AI Client SDK (0.9.0) — gemini-2.5-flash	Combines local EXIF/ELA telemetry with multimodal vision and text analysis to output structured JSON forensic scores and reconstruct the baseline source.
2. Data Flow & Forensic Pipeline
1. Ingestion Layer:
    * Accepts inputs via in-app OutlinedTextField / ActivityResultContracts.GetContent() picker, or externally via Intent.ACTION_SEND (text/plain and image/* MIME filters in AndroidManifest.xml).
    * Downscales high-resolution bitmaps (loadScaledBitmap capped at 960px max dimension) to prevent OutOfMemoryError and optimize upload payload size.
2. Local Edge Pre-Processing (Dispatchers.IO):
    * Step A (EXIF Scan): Parses the ContentResolver input stream for camera hardware signatures and editing software tags.
    * Step B (Error Level Analysis): Compresses the bitmap into an in-memory ByteArrayOutputStream at 90% JPEG quality, computes the absolute RGB channel difference against the original bitmap (abs(c1 - c2) * 20), generates the visual heatmap Bitmap, and calculates a mean variance score.
3. Multimodal Cloud Reasoning & Ground-Truth Reconstruction:
    * Bundles the scaled bitmap, user text, EXIF telemetry string, and ELA variance score into a deterministic prompt enforcing a strict 11-field JSON schema (ForensicResult).
    * Parses the response via org.json.JSONObject and updates the Jetpack Compose UI state.
3. Build Configuration & Cloud CI/CD Pipeline
During development, project structure and compilation were standardized for zero-lag cloud builds:
* Gradle Hierarchy Resolution: Separated root-level plugin declarations (build.gradle.kts (Project: Be_Original)) from module-level dependencies (app/build.gradle.kts (Module :app)). 
* Cloud Offloading (GitHub Codespaces & GitHub Actions):
    * Configured .github/workflows/android-cloud-build.yml running on ubuntu-latest with Eclipse Temurin JDK 17 and automated Gradle caching.
    * Executes ./gradlew assembleDebug on every push to main/master or manual workflow_dispatch, publishing BeOriginal-debug-apk (app-debug.apk) directly as a downloadable build artifact.
4. Security & Pre-Release Checklist (Next Engineering Milestones)
Before publishing Be Original to production on the Google Play Store, complete these three hardening tasks:
1. API Key Obfuscation / Backend Proxy: Move GEMINI_API_KEY out of MainActivity.kt into local.properties via the secrets-gradle-plugin for internal testing, and transition to Firebase App Check / Vertex AI in Firebase or a lightweight proxy for public Play Store release.
2. Release Signing & R8 Minification: Add a production keystore signature block and enable isMinifyEnabled = true in app/build.gradle.kts with ProGuard rules for org.json and the Generative AI SDK.
3. C2PA Cryptographic Manifest Support: Integrate c2pa-rs (via JNI/Rust bindings) in v1.1 to cryptographically validate hardware-signed Content Credentials alongside EXIF and ELA checks.
